Commands used to clone the GitHub repository and push changes:
1. Clone the GitHub repository using SSH
git clone git@github.com:HovorkovaH/ci2.git
2. Navigate to the local repository
cd ci2
3. Commit the changes with a meaningful message
git commit -a -m "Update project files"
4. Verify the latest commit
git log -1 --oneline
5. Push the changes to GitHub
git push
